<refentry version="5.1"
  xml:id="Api.SilikoNodeAssign"
  xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook">
<refmeta>
  <refentrytitle>SilikoNodeAssign</refentrytitle>
</refmeta>

<refnamediv>
  <refname><function>SilikoNodeAssign</function></refname>
  <refpurpose>Set the value of a node to match another</refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<programlisting language="C">#include &lt;SilikoCore/Node.h&gt;</programlisting>
<programlisting language="C">void SilikoNodeAssign(
    SilikoNode *object,
    const SilikoNode *right_side);</programlisting>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsection>
<title>Description</title>
<para>The <function>SilikoNodeAssign</function> function assigns the
value of <varname>right_side</varname> to the object that
<varname>object</varname> points to. If <varname>object</varname>
previously had child nodes, they are passed to
<function>SilikoNodeDestroy</function>. If
<varname>right_side</varname> has child elements, then a deep copy is
made when copying the values to <varname>object</varname>.</para>
</refsection>
</refentry>
